\section{Snowball Paper Enrichment}

When fetching references or citations from providers like WOS, we often get
incomplete metadata---particularly missing titles. This function enriches
snowball papers by looking up their DOIs in other providers.

Unlike regular enrichment (which assumes we have a title and want the abstract),
snowball enrichment focuses on papers that may lack basic metadata like titles.
We try to resolve as much as possible using the DOI.

<<enrichment functions>>=
def enrich_snowball_papers(
    papers: list[Paper],
    progress_callback: Callable[[int, int], None] | None = None,
) -> list[Paper]:
    """
    Enrich papers from snowballing (refs/cites) that may lack titles.

    This function is specifically designed for papers returned by citation
    or reference lookups, which often have incomplete metadata. It attempts
    to resolve missing titles and other fields using DOI lookups.

    Papers without DOIs or that cannot be enriched are returned as-is.
    Papers without titles after enrichment are filtered out.

    Args:
        papers: List of papers to enrich (typically from refs/cites lookup).
        progress_callback: Called with (current, total) after each paper.

    Returns:
        List of enriched papers. Papers without titles are excluded.
    """
    logger.info(f"Enriching {len(papers)} snowball papers")

    result = []
    total = len(papers)

    for i, paper in enumerate(papers):
        enriched = paper

        # If paper lacks a title but has a DOI, try to enrich it
        if (not paper.title or paper.title.strip() == "") and paper.doi:
            enriched = enrich_paper(paper, fields=["title", "abstract", "authors"])

        # Only include papers that have titles after enrichment
        if enriched.title and enriched.title.strip():
            result.append(enriched)
        else:
            logger.debug(f"Skipping paper without title (DOI: {paper.doi})")

        if progress_callback:
            progress_callback(i + 1, total)

    logger.info(f"Snowball enrichment: {len(result)}/{total} papers have titles")
    return result
